# PLANK metrics through Telegraf

Branch: `metrics-telegraf`, based on accepted main `1d770bab`.

The operator wants Host and Client metrics in an existing InfluxDB 2 bucket
and an existing Grafana instance. The operator chose to retain InfluxDB 2. Linux Hosts and Ubuntu Clients already run
Telegraf. Macs do not yet have the agent. Deployment addresses, organization,
bucket and credentials stay in private notes/provisioning, outside this repo.

## Architecture

PLANK emits bounded Influx line-protocol datagrams to an IPv4 loopback listener.
Use Telegraf's built-in `inputs.socket_listener` and the existing
`outputs.influxdb_v2`; no custom Telegraf plugin, database SDK, credential store,
new PLANK transport lane, or externally listening PLANK service is needed.
The same exporter supports both operating systems. Mac collection requires a
separate Telegraf installation; PLANK packages do not install/start that agent.

Administrator configuration in Host/Client INI files enables metrics, selects
the localhost UDP port (default 28991) and sample interval (default 1 second).
Disabled by default. Export failures never fail or delay a session. No HTTP,
DNS, disk spooling, synchronous retry or per-frame network logging in PLANK.
Telegraf owns buffering and remote delivery. The local datagram hop is best
effort, not a reliable audit trail. No extra privileges are required.

## Data and dashboard

- Reuse transport counters and Client decoder/presenter statistics. Keep
  sender drops, receive queue drops, frame gaps, QUIC loss and RaptorQ source-
  symbol loss separate. Do not export the toolbar's ten-second peaks as raw
  interval loss. Handle counter resets and unknown/empty intervals explicitly.
- Export RTT, video/audio rates and counts, queue pressure/drops, network/
  decode/render FPS, processing/decoding/presentation timing, stream profile,
  capture source, resolution, and metric freshness where actually available.
  Do not invent unavailable capture/encoder/GPU or audio-device measurements.
- Telegraf adds its existing local `host` tag so PLANK and system metrics can
  be correlated. Stable workstation/bookmark identifiers distinguish peers and
  duplicate bookmarks. Highly variable connection identifiers remain fields.
- Keep schema names and units fixed; bound fields, strings and datagrams.
  No usernames, credentials, clipboard text, keystrokes or screen contents.
  Emit wall-clock timestamps; calculate rates with monotonic elapsed time.
- Supply a Grafana dashboard with a selectable existing InfluxDB data source,
  existing InfluxQL queries, machine/session filters, network/FEC, video, queue/drop and freshness panels.
  Reuse system metrics already collected by Telegraf instead of duplicating them.

## Provisioning and qualification

The existing Ubuntu installer copies selected Telegraf drop-ins. Its output and
token are already configured; add only the PLANK input when integrating that
separate provisioning repository. Current flush interval 5s plus jitter 10s means
samples reach the database in batches roughly 5–15s apart. Preserve this policy
unless the operator requests a change; source samples can still be one second.

Test line-protocol escaping/types, payload limits, resets, empty intervals,
disabled mode, absent/stalled collectors, concurrent teardown and multiple
sessions. Exercise the real Telegraf parser with an isolated localhost listener
and file output. Keep streaming/loss performance limits unchanged. Build all
four candidates on hosted Actions and preserve the accepted main baseline.

The dashboard is deployed against the existing InfluxQL data source; all 34
queries are accepted. The operator authorized Linux-only deployment. Both Linux
products and local Telegraf inputs are installed and enabled. Real Host metrics
are visible; Client media collection awaits the operator's reconnection. The
Host's system-metrics bucket is preserved through an application-only output
filter and its existing route to the same database. No Mac deployment occurred.
No merge, release publication or change to existing system-metric collection
is implied by creating this branch.
